course: dictionary
lesson: 9176
title: Snugly: warm and close
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: «Snugly» is an adverb, made from the adjective «snug». It tells you how something is done. It has two meanings, and both are about being close and safe. In a story, a child tucked snugly in bed is warm, cosy and comfortable.
explain: The other meaning is about fit. «A bike helmet must fit snugly, sit level just above the eyebrows and have the strap buckled; a loose helmet does not protect.» Here snugly means fitting closely with no gaps, but not too tight. A loose helmet is the opposite: it moves about and does not protect your head.
explain: Look at the words around snugly to decide which meaning fits. Words such as bed, blanket or burrow point to comfort. Words such as fit, buckled or strap point to a close fit. Then try your meaning in the sentence: if it still makes sense, you have it.
fact: «Snugly» means in a warm, comfortable and cosy way.
fact: «Snugly» also means fitting closely and tightly, with no gaps, but not too tight.
fact: «Snug» is the adjective, and adding -ly turns it into the adverb «snugly».
fact: A helmet that fits snugly sits close on the head with no gaps.
fact: A bike helmet should sit level, about two fingers above the eyebrows, with the strap buckled snugly.
exercise: «The child was tucked snugly in bed under a thick quilt.» What does snugly mean here? | In a loud and noisy way | Far away from the bed | Quickly and without any care | *In a warm, cosy way
exercise: «A bike helmet must fit snugly, sit level just above the eyebrows and have the strap buckled.» What does snugly mean here? | Very fast | Hanging loose and wobbling about | *Fitting closely with no gaps, but not too tight | Painted in bright colours
exercise: Ella says a helmet should fit snugly. Which helmet fits snugly? | *A helmet that sits close on the head with no gaps | A helmet that wobbles when you shake your head | A helmet with the strap left undone | A helmet that is far too big and falls over your eyes
test: «The kitten curled up snugly in its basket by the fire.» What does snugly suggest about the kitten? | Lost and frightened | Hungry and cold | Running fast | *Warm and comfortable
test: «The lid should fit snugly on the box, with no gaps.» What does snugly mean here? | Hanging open | Painted red | Very noisy | *Fitting closely with no gaps, but not too tight
exam: Which sentence uses snugly to mean warm and cosy? | *«The baby slept snugly under her soft blanket.» | «The door swung snugly open in the storm.» | «She ran snugly to the bus stop.» | «The wind blew snugly through the tall trees.»
